    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi saw that adding two even numbers always gave an even number.\n\"Is that always true?\" he asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "parity",
     "even",
     "odd"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Parity tells whether a whole number is even or odd. Even plus even is even, odd plus odd is even and even plus odd is odd.\nThe sum of the first n odd numbers is n squared. We can see this by arranging small squares in a grid.\nParity of expressions: 2n is always even and 2n plus 1 is always odd for any whole number n."
    }
   },
